			<div class="content" id="post-content-4492228">
									

<p>I adore this. A compelling, if not particularly obscure, mystery, a competent foundation, a powerful message, and some very cool ideas. I was engaged throughout the whole piece, which considering the length is saying something. +1</p>
<p>Only real issue I have with it is the Alexandria connection is too tenuous and obscure. As is, it just seems like the civilization discrepancy is an unexplained aspect of the mystery that never gets developed. There is only payoff if the reader is deeply familiar with 4001 and you as an author, and even then it is easily missable without reading the comments here.</p>

